{
  "name": "nearest_hit_ties",
  "description": "Hits whose t differ by no more than 1e-9 mm are a tie, and the component earlier in the list wins. Pairs of 40 mm detectors at 225 degrees with collinear, overlapping surfaces (centres 10 mm apart along the surface) are crossed by one beam each at a single point: the pairs a0..a3 / b0..b3 are listed B then A (L0..L3 must end at b0..b3; without the tolerance the last bit of t made them end at a0..a3), a4/b4 and a5/b5 are listed A then B (a4, a5). L6 meets two detectors at the very same place: s2, the earlier one in the list. L7 meets 'near' (0.01 mm nearer) although 'far' is listed first: a real difference is not a tie.",
  "layout": {
